  "description": "The security scan of the Python package **requests** version **2.26.0** (identified as *pypi:requests:2.26.0*) was completed successfully, adhering to the **cvecheck_results** schema version **2\u20110\u20110** (see\u202fhttps://example.com/schemas/cvecheck_results-v2-0-0.json for reference).\n\nTwo vulnerabilities were detected. **CVE\u20112023\u201112345** (CWE\u201120) allows remote code execution due to improper input validation. It can be exploited over the network with no authentication required, low attack complexity, and a network attack vector. The impact is rated as partial loss of availability, complete compromise of confidentiality, and partial loss of integrity, yielding a CVSS score of **7.8**. Further details are available at https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-12345 and https://security-advisories.example.com/CVE-2023-12345.  \n\nThe second issue, **CVE\u20112022\u20116789** (CWE\u201179), is a cross\u2011site scripting (XSS) flaw in the web interface. Exploitation requires a single authentication step, medium complexity, and an adjacent\u2011network vector. Its impact includes no loss of availability, partial loss of confidentiality, and complete loss of integrity, with a CVSS score of **5.3**. The advisory can be consulted at https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2022-6789.\n\nOverall, the scan completed with **2 vulnerabilities found**, and all identified issues fall into the medium to high severity range."
